Fix micro-cuts on looping sounds: use AICA hardware loop.

ALdc implemented looping in software: when a looping source (e.g. the BFG
hum or railgun recharge) reached the end of its buffer, the device thread
stopped the channel, freed it, allocated it again and re-issued START. Each
cycle leaves a silence gap up to the poll interval, so looping sounds cut
out periodically.

The AICA can loop a channel in hardware (chan->loop=1, loopstart/loopend).
Use it for looping sources and skip the software time-based switch, so the
channel runs continuously without gaps. play_channel()/play_channels() gain
a loop flag.
